{
  "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
  "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Stephen B. Bright)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The decision here of the majority of the Louisiana Supreme Court on remand from this Court is an extraordinary departure from the lessons that this Court taught in its Miller-El decisions. And I point out sort of three overarching errors in that regard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Can I ask you about one of the factors?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there were five African-American jurors who were the subject of prosecutorial peremptory challenges."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, suppose you are trying this case. You are a defense attorney, and you ask a juror, a potential juror: Would you hold it against a defendant who doesn't take the stand? And the initial answer is: I have to think about that. I'm not quite sure."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Bright, the Judge was quite passive, and was -- was the judge, in fact, present throughout the entire voir dire?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Defense",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The defense moves to ask to quit referring to the O. J. Simpson case in the media; and, for goodness sakes, Judge, don't let him refer to it before the jury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you believe that, if there had been a white defendant here, the O. J. Simpson case would have been mentioned?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Before -- before the rebuttal, this prosecutor was going around advertising this as his O. J. Simpson case, and the defense attorney said please, Judge, get him to stop saying that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well, do you -- do you believe that it would have been appropriate at that point for the prosecutor to invoke in his argument any case from any state in which a criminal defendant had unsuccessfully feigned insanity as a reason to decide -- for the jurors to decide that this defendant is -- is feigning insanity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What's the difference between that and \"okay\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask you about Juror Hawkins. You haven't talked much about him."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Boudreaux",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BOUDREAUX: The back strike is when is the challenge exercised. In and of itself you can't say if it is racial or not. It is a challenge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Boudreaux",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "African-Americans are 20 percent of the population of Jefferson Parish, but they were less than 11 percent of the people summoned for jury duty."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: So what could you --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bright",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BRIGHT: But the reason for doing that would be to have the judge not allow the strike and to put that juror in the box and the juror' gone now. So that, as a practical matter, is not going to work."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bright",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BRIGHT: But there's no procedural rule in Louisiana that says you have to do that. It might have been a stronger case if they had done it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-10119",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0f451372774f349e3f7d6d76a1d51d832a9f3ff40619c9cb87dfa9b13e8ef882",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0f451372774f-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
